# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — what NEVER goes to git.
#
# Anything regenerable (deps, build output) or per-install state
# (database, logs, OAuth tokens, encryption keys) is excluded. Code,
# config templates, docs, and migrations ARE tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# dependencies (regenerable via pnpm install)
/node_modules
/.pnpm-store

# build artifacts (regenerable via pnpm build)
/.next
/dist
/out
/build
/coverage
.turbo
.vercel
.swc

# TypeScript build incremental files
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# OS metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# IDE state (per-developer; share via the repo's own configs instead)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Certificates / signing
*.pem
*.key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# USER DATA — NEVER commit. Each install creates its own.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SQLite database + WAL / shared-memory + auto-backups
data.db
data.db-shm
data.db-wal
data.db.bak
data.db.bak-*
# Anything at all that looks like a copy of the user's database. The
# patterns above only covered the .bak naming the in-app backup uses; a
# hand-made copy called data.db.backup-whatever slipped straight past
# them and into `git add -A`.
data.db*.backup*
data.db-*.backup*
*.db.backup*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
/data/

# Tool-generated user assets (screenshots, exports, PDFs, etc.)
/public/uploads/
/screenshots/
/exports/

# OAuth refresh tokens / API-key encryption key — leakage = account compromise
.seo-encryption-key
# Signs session cookies. Committing it would let anyone who reads the
# repo mint a valid session for any user id on any install built from it.
.seo-session-secret

# Per-instance runtime state
.seo-port
# One word, "docker" or "native" — the answer the control panel asks for
# when Docker is installed but not running, so it only asks once. Per
# machine, so it must not travel with the repo.
.seo-install-mode
dev-server.log
dev-server.err.log
.dev-server.pid
.dev-server.cmd
.install-progress
# Junk files that have accidentally slipped in via bash heredoc /
# commit-message parsing in past sessions. Keeping them explicitly
# ignored so re-occurrences never get staged.
commit-msg.txt
/dev
/production
/3000)
/hard)

# Logs in general
*.log

# Redis dump (if Redis worker writes locally)
dump.rdb

# Desktop guides regenerated per install
*-Welcome.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — NEVER commit.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Note: .env.example IS tracked — it's the documented template.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-user tool config (Claude Code, scheduled-task locks, etc.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/

# Internal project plan / Claude Code context — strategy, decision log,
# competitive analysis, pricing notes, validation outreach. Kept locally
# for the maintainer + Claude Code to reference; never committed.
CLAUDE.md
.e2e/

# Playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Backups made by the control panel. These are copies of data.db and
# contain everything — clients, audits, and encrypted API keys. They
# must never be committed.
backups/

# Built plugin archives stay out — EXCEPT the one people download.
#
# The WordPress bridge has to be installable by someone who is not going
# to clone a repository: WordPress only accepts a .zip, and the docs
# used to point at a bare .php path, which its upload form rejects. So
# seo-tool-bridge.zip is committed, and gets a direct raw.githubusercontent
# URL from the README and from inside the app.
#
# Committing a binary is only safe with something holding it to its
# source. `plugin-zip.test.ts` compares the PHP inside the zip against
# the PHP beside it, byte for byte — the previous hand-built archive sat
# at v0.6.0 for six weeks while the source said v0.6.1, and nothing
# noticed. Rebuild with: node scripts/build-plugin-zip.mjs
wordpress-plugin/*.zip
!wordpress-plugin/seo-tool-bridge.zip

# Built docs site — regenerate with `node docs-site/build.mjs`
/docs-site/dist

# Internal planning and strategy notes. scripts/build-release-zip.mjs
# already excluded these from the user download as "notes to ourselves";
# they were still published on the public repo, and the competitive review
# directly contradicted the CLAUDE.md note above, which says competitive
# analysis is kept locally and never committed. The one publicly useful
# conclusion from the MCP plan (a chat subscription cannot stand in for an
# API key, and why) now lives in the README FAQ.
docs/competitive-review-*.md
docs/mcp-connections-plan.md

# Audit prompts for whoever is reviewing this next. Useful to run, but
# notes to ourselves rather than documentation — scripts/build-release-zip.mjs
# already excluded them from the user download on exactly that reasoning.
docs/audits/

# Auto-generated agent instructions (a BEGIN/END stub pointing at a guide
# inside node_modules). The hand-written agent context, CLAUDE.md, is
# already local-only; publishing a generated stub while hiding the real
# thing was the inconsistency.
docs/AGENTS.md

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/

# Blog drafts written for "Open in Claude" (regenerable from the review queue).
/.seo-drafts/
